  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/426659329/@cloudflare/workers-utils@0.57.0</id>
    <updated>2026-11-23T19:24:26Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/releases/tag/%40cloudflare%2Fworkers-utils%400.57.0"/>
    <title>@cloudflare/workers-utils@0.57.0</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h3&gt;Minor Changes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/pull/16879&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/cloudflare/workers-sdk/pull/16879/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16879&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/commit/5970e6a842b36665ab092f54ae276d34b02e3a29&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;5970e6a&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Thanks &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/edmundhung&quot;&gt;@edmundhung&lt;/a&gt;! - Add &lt;code&gt;readD1Migrations()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;applyD1Migrations()&lt;/code&gt; for reading and applying D1 migrations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These move from the Vitest plugin so other tools apply migrations the same way. &lt;code&gt;readD1Migrations()&lt;/code&gt; is available from the main entry point and throws when the migrations directory is missing. &lt;code&gt;applyD1Migrations()&lt;/code&gt; is available from the &lt;code&gt;apply-d1-migrations&lt;/code&gt; entry point, which has no Node.js imports so it runs inside workerd, and it also accepts the D1 binding from Miniflare&#39;s &lt;code&gt;getD1Database()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Patch Changes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/pull/17070&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/cloudflare/workers-sdk/pull/17070/hovercard&quot;&gt;#17070&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/commit/657179d3d707a244038168675292b288e0a1f4ef&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;657179d&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Thanks &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apps/dependabot&quot;&gt;@dependabot&lt;/a&gt;! - Update &lt;code&gt;DEFAULT_COMPAT_DATE&lt;/code&gt; to 2026-11-23&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use the bundled workerd release&#39;s compatibility date by default when scaffolding new projects or when no compatibility date is configured.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/pull/17078&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/cloudflare/workers-sdk/pull/17078/hovercard&quot;&gt;#17078&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/commit/b00799168dc2580013ea3c9b7d4f4505e120afa2&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;b007991&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Thanks &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/petebacondarwin&quot;&gt;@petebacondarwin&lt;/a&gt;! - Recover from missing Worker scripts after an interrupted first deploy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When the Workers API returns a service without a script, &lt;code&gt;wrangler deploy&lt;/code&gt; uses the first-deploy flow instead of crashing. &lt;code&gt;wrangler versions upload&lt;/code&gt; tells you to run &lt;code&gt;wrangler deploy&lt;/code&gt; first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>petebacondarwin</name>
    </author>
